From da5e46ac9a729a6e0b7cc08f091bad293ede4f42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Utkarsh Vats <uvats_be23@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 22:43:08 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] run_subscribe_msckf: exit without unwinding to avoid a
 shutdown race

use_multi_threading_subs is hardcoded true, so every IMU callback detaches
a thread that runs the VIO update inside VioManager. On SIGINT the executor
returns on the main thread, which then runs the global viz/sys destructors
while a detached update thread can still be mid-update, locking a just-freed
camera_queue_mtx. glibc aborts with a pthread_mutex_lock assertion (SIGABRT)
on every shutdown on this aarch64 Jetson.

rclcpp is already shut down and nothing is left to flush by the end of main,
so flush stdio and std::_Exit() instead of returning into static destruction.
Estimator output is unchanged (stage1_axes replay: 1.15% drift, identical
across 3 runs); the process now exits cleanly.

Local Jetson patch, not for upstream as-is (the real fix is joinable
subscriber threads).
---
 ov_msckf/src/run_subscribe_msckf.cpp | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ov_msckf/src/run_subscribe_msckf.cpp b/ov_msckf/src/run_subscribe_msckf.cpp
index 6a5b341..b4676b6 100644
--- a/ov_msckf/src/run_subscribe_msckf.cpp
+++ b/ov_msckf/src/run_subscribe_msckf.cpp
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
  * along with this program.  If not, see <https://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.
  */
 
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <memory>
 
 #include "core/VioManager.h"
@@ -121,5 +122,13 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv) {
 #endif
 
   // Done!
+  // The async IMU-callback update thread (use_multi_threading_subs, hardcoded true above)
+  // is detached and can still be mid-update inside VioManager when executor.spin()
+  // returns on SIGINT. Running the global viz/sys destructors here races that thread
+  // onto a just-freed mutex -> glibc pthread_mutex assertion / SIGABRT. rclcpp is
+  // already shut down and there is nothing left to flush, so exit without unwinding.
+  std::cout.flush();
+  std::cerr.flush();
+  std::_Exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);
   return EXIT_SUCCESS;
 }
